# Local data and security

- User sources and learner history stay local.
- API keys use OS-protected credential storage — never renderer or SQLite.
- Source content is untrusted data. Prompt injection in PDFs, pages, transcripts, and notes must not affect tool policy.
- Provider requests contain only required context.
- No telemetry leaves the machine unless a developer explicitly opts in.
- No key, source content, or learner information in ordinary logs.
